func unescapeDouble(s string) string {
	// handle \" \\ \n \t \r etc, but keep \( for interpolation? Actually \( is interpolation, not escape. So `\(` should remain as `\(` for later parsing? Our lexer kept `\(` as two chars `\` + `(`? In lex for double strings, we kept `\` + next char as is (wrote both). So `\(` remains `\(`. Good. For other escapes, unescape.
