			usage = getCompletionUsage()
		} else {
			usage = getText("root_usage.txt")
			// root_usage.txt ends with \n\n (extra blank). For flag errors, original root usage ends with single \n? Let's check: flag error output ends with "...Will default to true in late 2025\n\n"? Actually error output we saw ends with "...\n\n"? The help ends with "...\n\n"? Root help ends with single \n, root usage ends with \n\n. For flag errors, which one is shown? Error output ends with "...\n\n"? Let's assume root_usage (with \n\n) is correct for errors? Actually `unknown flag` error shows usage with ...? The captured error output ends with "...\n\n"? Hard to tell. We'll use root_usage as is.
		}
